      "body": "<!-- markdownlint-disable -->\n\n## Overview\n\nDuring `pause_generation(mode=\"wait\")` (`PAUSED_NEW`), `get_num_unfinished_requests()` counts `kv_holding_waiting` but subtracts every paused streaming session. A session that stopped while preempted (kept since #58778) holds no blocks and sits in `waiting`, so subtracting it cancels out a running request. The engine goes idle and the pause completes with that request unfinished; with the default `clear_cache=True` the cache reset then preempts it.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Under `PAUSED_NEW`, paused sessions are skipped inside `kv_holding_waiting` instead of subtracted from it, so the count can't drop below the requests that still drain. `UNPAUSED` counting is unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nNew scheduler test, next to the existing `PAUSED_NEW` count tests:\n\n```\n$ pytest tests/v1/core/test_scheduler.py::test_pause_new_counts_running_request_beside_preempted_session\n# base c50aca144:  assert 0 == 1  (where 0 = get_num_unfinished_requests())\n# with fix:        PASSED\n\n$ pytest tests/v1/core/test_scheduler.py tests/v1/core/test_async_scheduler.py tests/v1/streaming_input/test_scheduler_streaming.py\n# base:      56 failed, 230 passed\n# with fix:  55 failed, 231 passed\n```\n\nThe only difference is the new test. The 55 shared failures are multimodal tests that fail in my local env on `LlavaForConditionalGeneration` inspection, with or without this change.\n\nReaching the state needs a streaming session preempted under KV pressure while its last step is in flight, which the scheduler test sets up directly, as #58778's tests do.\n\n## Details\n\nIntroduced by the combination of #60572 (counts only `kv_holding_waiting` under `PAUSED_NEW`) and #58778 (keeps sessions that stop while preempted, with `num_computed_tokens == 0`, so they're enqueued in `waiting`). The new sum walks `kv_holding_waiting` only while paused; that queue holds requests with allocated blocks, so it stays small.\n\nNo open issue or PR covers this (searched `get_num_unfinished_requests pause`, `kv_holding_waiting`). AI assistance (Claude Code) was used; I reviewed the change and ran the tests locally.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
